# An omen card may be cast as its Omen wherever the card may be cast (CR 720.3, 601.3), not only from the hand. On turn 3
# Bot1 casts Coil and Catch from the hand, draws three (another Marang River Regent among them) and discards that Regent.
# On turn 5, with mana for {3}{U} open, nothing yet lets Bot1 cast from its graveyard, so the Regent there offers no cast at
# all; then Yawgmoth's Will ("you may play lands and cast spells from your graveyard") does, and Bot1 casts Coil and Catch
# from the graveyard. It resolves: Bot1 draws three and discards an Island, which Yawgmoth's Will exiles instead, and Coil
# and Catch is shuffled into the library (CR 720.3d) - it was not going to the graveyard, so Yawgmoth's Will does not exile
# it. Every count holds whatever the shuffles did: the library is 19 cards less 7, the two draws and the six cards the two
# Omens drew, plus the two Regents shuffled back in, 6.

